<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:42Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Dozens missing as deadly fire hits Indonesian candy factory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3696ca82165e3bb9395c5bda3cc73817f2756aeac22cf6c0b97c0bafd3cb6c19</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T06:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dozens-missing-as-deadly-fire-hits-indonesian-candy-factory/a-80012342--07c7cd5dbdea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dozens-missing-as-deadly-fire-hits-indonesian-candy-factory/a-80012342?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A fire at a confectionery factory in Indonesia's Banten province has killed at least three people. Dozens are also unaccounted for after the blaze, which destroyed large parts of the facility.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russian helicopter suspected of violating Finnish airspace</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb0a512386c4165229ecfb823ea4db599f2aa9e197f17fb3841179e05a5d9f0f</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:07:51Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T17:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russian-helicopter-suspected-of-violating-finnish-airspace/a-80010133--74b233a91706.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russian-helicopter-suspected-of-violating-finnish-airspace/a-80010133?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Finland's Defense Ministry thinks the incursion is linked to a drone strike earlier Saturday on a Russian cargo ship, which is on a US sanctions list.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU and Indonesia sign trade deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02a335ba04d9350b83ea6cb07bfecb217ca01ea7274bcca8e98e30864ebc87c8</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:07:51Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T15:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-and-indonesia-sign-trade-deal/a-80010099--bb068ad239d4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-and-indonesia-sign-trade-deal/a-80010099?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A deal covering 730 million people promises lower tariffs and new investment opportunities as the European Union seeks to diversify trade ties amid growing global economic tensions.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>New EU budget proposal aims at tax gobal tech giants</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b8b6c414ef8f4767f4ed8f80667bacc26506d726e8cda0997ce8814672937708</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:07:51Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T14:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/new-eu-budget-proposal-aims-at-tax-gobal-tech-giants/a-80009255--8ff3ddfff270.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/new-eu-budget-proposal-aims-at-tax-gobal-tech-giants/a-80009255?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">European Council President Antonio Costa has proposed a smaller EU budget for 2028-2034, including a 3% tax on major digital firms to ease member states' contributions. France has already rejected the plan as inadequate.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Russia strikes Zelenskyy's hometown, killing 2</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:30bf6f094117acc05f01cfbbb03e9ae2907a978fcca4f4c4cf7f825cd734ebcb</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:07:51Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T14:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-strikes-zelenskyy-s-hometown-killing-2/a-80009458--1c5b88d83c35.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-strikes-zelenskyy-s-hometown-killing-2/a-80009458?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The attacks follow Russian President Vladimir Putin's vow of a "painful" response to Ukraine's attacks this week on the Kerch Bridge, linking Russian-occupied Crimea.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Anthropic researcher uses AI to solve math's greatest riddle</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:496cc1118362e98e80bb615485fee59660b9625e6a5c1f25180c733274b24351</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:07:51Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T10:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/anthropic-researcher-uses-ai-to-solve-math-s-greatest-riddle/a-80008428--770513448c0a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/anthropic-researcher-uses-ai-to-solve-math-s-greatest-riddle/a-80008428?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The proposed breakthrough could reshape mathematical research, but still needs independent verification. It's the latest in a string of cases where AI has outpaced humans in solving famous maths problems.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Man convicted of arson over deadly 2025 Palisades fire in Los Angeles</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5be0bb01636f728cd0610d0d0ca1dbbb27c561ab5312f0c10978e1a0f6fb390b</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:07:51Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T07:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/man-convicted-of-arson-over-deadly-2025-palisades-fire-in-los-angeles/a-80007933--9f183d2c9cc1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/man-convicted-of-arson-over-deadly-2025-palisades-fire-in-los-angeles/a-80007933?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A 30-year-old man has been convicted of causing one of the most destructive wildfires in the history of Los Angeles. The verdict came after the case was retried.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil ex-President Jair Bolsonaro taken to hospital over abdominal pain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d8e6616ecfe4c6cbf117f4826f9d563acc652e946c65ccc89181ed36d5ff5a1</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:07:51Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T03:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brazil-ex-president-jair-bolsonaro-taken-to-hospital-over-abdominal-pain/a-80007648--e735cc923d74.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brazil-ex-president-jair-bolsonaro-taken-to-hospital-over-abdominal-pain/a-80007648?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jair Bolsonaro has been hospitalized in Brasilia with intestinal obstruction. The former far-right Brazilian leader is receiving pain medications, his son Carlos said.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Russian ornithologist jailed over small donations to Navalny's foundation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5f0ecf869643130d77bd6916501223c9a9bf9865a599577ba98a1541c7796e7e</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:07:51Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T20:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russian-ornithologist-jailed-over-small-donations-to-navalny-s-foundation/a-80005505--49dba4e1f94e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russian-ornithologist-jailed-over-small-donations-to-navalny-s-foundation/a-80005505?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Sofia Rosenfeld has devoted her life to studying Arctic birds. A Russian court sentenced her to 3.5 years in a penal colony over donations to Navalny's foundation. Friends and family are fighting for her release.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Repression against Iranian lawyers increases</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d16f0d68132097d8b5891bed0bfe0af563be74c075bb3a9c08e9180dcbdaa901</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:07:51Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T20:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/repression-against-iranian-lawyers-increases/a-80006742--c2e9244e707c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/repression-against-iranian-lawyers-increases/a-80006742?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At least 135 lawyers in Iran have been subjected to repressive measures over the past year. UN experts warn that this seriously jeopardizes the right of those accused to trial in a constitutional court.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Is Pakistan backing anti-Taliban groups in Afghanistan?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:effff15f11532eed9bcd2d881c3b0b434df708c96e3604e7618cc3ba7465e4f0</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:07:51Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T15:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-pakistan-backing-anti-taliban-groups-in-afghanistan/a-80004814--1a7b1c3175b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-pakistan-backing-anti-taliban-groups-in-afghanistan/a-80004814?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Taliban rulers in Afghanistan have accused Pakistan of aiding and sheltering armed resistance groups. The allegations come amid heightened tensions and are likely to deepen the rift between the two neighbors.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU and UK strike 'landmark deal' to strengthen ties after Brexit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19190f3535698f8673e9a2ed68db0ccce0722295d6bffabe21852613a46ee2c7</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:07:51Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T14:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-and-uk-strike-landmark-deal-to-strengthen-ties-after-brexit/a-80001076--f12586fcea84.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-and-uk-strike-landmark-deal-to-strengthen-ties-after-brexit/a-80001076?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Union and the United Kingdom have agreed on "landmark" deals on youth mobility and trade. Leaders on both sides praised the agreement as they seek to rebuild ties.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
